description:
In smime-tree/src/encrypt.rs, ecdh_wrap_cek() derives a key-encryption key (KEK) into a plain Vec<u8>:

    let mut kek = vec![0u8; kek_len];
    ansi_x963_kdf::derive_key_into::<D>(shared_secret_bytes, &shared_info_der, &mut kek)?;
    // kek used to wrap CEK, then dropped with no zeroization

The KEK is derived from the ECDH shared secret and used once to wrap the CEK. After use it is dropped as a plain Vec<u8>, leaving key material on the heap until the allocator reclaims the region.

Review pass 6 correctly zeroized the CEK via Zeroizing<Vec<u8>> in encrypt_aes_cbc(). The KEK in ecdh_wrap_cek() was not addressed in that pass.

Fix: declare kek as Zeroizing<Vec<u8>>:

    let mut kek = Zeroizing::new(vec![0u8; kek_len]);

Zeroizing implements DerefMut so the KDF call (needs &mut [u8]) and the AES-KW slice (needs &[u8; N]) continue to work unchanged. zeroize is already a dependency.

Acceptance criteria:
- kek declared as Zeroizing<Vec<u8>> in ecdh_wrap_cek
- cargo test -p smime-tree passes
- cargo clippy -p smime-tree -- -D warnings passes
